WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.860
Your study is done.

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:04.050
One result becomes a sentence.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.250
ArxivChecker, a skill
for your AI assistant,

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.750
starts with the evidence,
not the old draft’s numbers.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.890
It traces the claim to its source,

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:18.260
and adds the comparison
and what’s left out.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.090
Figures come straight from the data.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.210
If a result goes missing, the build stops.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.540
The paper tells the story in order,
from the problem to its limits.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.320
It sets the paper in
LaTeX, and sorts the rules.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:42.600
arXiv asks for margins
of at least an inch.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.010
arXiv advises a description
for every figure.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.730
And your house style leaves
off the page numbers.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.830
Then it rebuilds the
paper in an empty folder,

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.080
from only the files you’ll send.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.440
You decide the names,

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.350
how AI was used, the license
and the final claims.
